concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-35 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "35 After section 52 of the Principal Act the following sections are inserted:"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-35 ;
    values:originalText "Australian Citizenship Amendment No. 129, 1984 Review of decisions \" 5 2 A . (1) Applications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for review of— (a) decisions of the Minister under section 13 or sub-section 23D ( 1 ) refusing an application; (b) decisions of the Minister under section 18 other than decisions under sub-section 18 (5); (c) decisions of the Minister under sub-section 21 (1) or 23 (2) or section 47; (d) decisions of the Minister, the Secretary, or a person authorized by the Secretary for the purposes of section 23A or 23B, under that section; and (e) decisions of the Minister under sub-section 23AA (2) refusing to register a declaration. \"(2) A person is not entitled to make an application under sub-section (1) for review of a decision under section 13 (other than sub-section 13 (9)) unless the person is a permanent resident. \"(3) In this section, 'decision' has the same meaning as in the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975. Statement to accompany notification of decisions \" 5 2 B . (1) Where the Minister or a delegate of a Minister makes a decision of the kind referred to in section 52A and gives, or causes to be given, to a person or persons whose interests are affected by the decision notice in writing of the decision, that notice shall include a statement to the effect that, subject to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 and to sub-section 52A (2) of this Act, application may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for review of the decision to which the notice relates by or on behalf of a person or persons whose interests are affected by the decision. \"(2) Any failure to comply with the requirements of sub-section (1) in relation to a decision does not affect the validity of the decision.\". Regulations" ;
    skos:definition "Australian Citizenship Amendment No. 129, 1984 Review of decisions \" 5 2 A . (1) Applications may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for review of— (a) decisions of the Minister under section 13 or sub-section 23D ( 1 ) refusing an application; (b) decisions of the Minister under section 18 other than decisions under sub-section 18 (5); (c) decisions of the Minister under sub-section 21 (1) or 23 (2) or section 47; (d) decisions of the Minister, the Secretary, or a person authorized by the Secretary for the purposes of section 23A or 23B, under that section; and (e) decisions of the Minister under sub-section 23AA (2) refusing to register a declaration. \"(2) A person is not entitled to make an application under sub-section (1) for review of a decision under section 13 (other than sub-section 13 (9)) unless the person is a permanent resident. \"(3) In this section, 'decision' has the same meaning as in the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975. Statement to accompany notification of decisions \" 5 2 B . (1) Where the Minister or a delegate of a Minister makes a decision of the kind referred to in section 52A and gives, or causes to be given, to a person or persons whose interests are affected by the decision notice in writing of the decision, that notice shall include a statement to the effect that, subject to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal Act 1975 and to sub-section 52A (2) of this Act, application may be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal for review of the decision to which the notice relates by or on behalf of a person or persons whose interests are affected by the decision. \"(2) Any failure to comply with the requirements of sub-section (1) in relation to a decision does not affect the validity of the decision.\". Regulations"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8c7fe15b5cae22430d164948bc70f012b06d4a9858ea5498dc836ec9d4fb7f2a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "21"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Applications for review of certain decisions can be made to the Administrative Appeals Tribunal." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984.pdf, p.21" ;
    cml:asserts concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-act-1984-sec-35-norm .
